      },
      "seq": 4,
      "text": "The first rule is: In the five minutes, players must work together to solve a mystery using the bell, pencil, and paper. They must communicate their ideas and write down clues on the paper. The first to correctly solve the mystery wins, but the game ends if the bell is rung more than three times. The winner gets a small prize. The loser must guess the mystery based on the clues written by the winner. The winner then reveals the solution. The game continues with the roles reversed for the next round. The loser gets to choose the next mystery clue type (e.g., historical fact, mathematical equation, etc.).\n\nWhat type of historical fact do you want to use for the next mystery clue?",
